<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cú Chulainn</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cuchulainn</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cú Chulainn is the greatest hero of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulster-cycle">Ulster Cycle</a> of Irish legend, a nephew of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conchobar-mac-nessa">Conchobar mac Nessa</a>. In the Táin Bó Cúailnge he defends Ulster single-handed against the army of Queen Medb of Connacht. He became a symbol of Irish nationalism, and a statue of his death stands in the General Post Office in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cu-chulainn.jpg" alt="Cú Chulainn" width="278" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stephen Reid · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cuslayshound.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
